{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":30,"type":"xterm-256color"},"timestamp":1791840230,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":"asciiverse/adventures/stories/stage/spider-and-web/spider-and-web","env":{"TERM":"xterm-256color","COLORTERM":"truecolor","LANG":"C.UTF-8"}}
[0.013, "o", "\u001b[?1049h\u001b[22;0;0t\u001b[1;30r\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[4l\u001b[?7h\u001b[?1h\u001b="]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m  End of Alley                                                                                      \u001b[3;1H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[mOn the whole, it was worth the trip. The plains really were broad and grain-gold, if scarred with\r\u001b[4dfences and agricultural crawlers. The mountains were overwhelming. And however much of the capital\r\u001b[5dcity is crusted with squat brick and faceless concrete hulks, there are still flashes of its\r\u001b[6d"]
[0.000, "o", "historic charm. You've seen spires above the streets -- tiny green parks below tenements -- hidden\r\u001b[7d"]
[0.000, "o", "jewels of fountains beyond walls. Any bland alley can conceal balconies wrought into iron gardens,\r\u001b[8d"]
[0.000, "o", "fiery mosaics, a tree or bed of flowers nurtured by who knows who.\r\u001b[10dThis alley, however, is a total washout. It ends in flat bare dirty brick, and you've found nothing\r\u001b[11d"]
[0.000, "o", "but a door which lacks even the courtesy of a handle. Maybe you should call it a day.\r\u001b[13d\u001b(B\u001b[0;1mSpider And Web\r\u001b[14d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[mInteractive Fiction\r\u001b[15d"]
[0.000, "o", "Copyright 1997-8 by Andrew Plotkin.\r\u001b[16d(First-time players should type \"about\". For credits, \"credits\".)\r\u001b[17d"]
[0.000, "o", "Release 4 / Serial number 980226 / Inform v6.14 Library 6/6\r\u001b[18dStandard interpreter 1.1\r\u001b[20d\u001b(B\u001b[0;1mEnd of Alley\r\u001b[21d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b(B\u001b[mIt's a narrow dead end here, with walls rising oppressively high in three directions. The alley is\r\u001b[22dquite empty, bare even of trash. (Your guidebook warned you: the police are as efficient about\r\u001b[23d"]
[0.000, "o", "litter laws as about everything else they do.) You can retreat to the south.\r\u001b[25d"]
[0.000, "o", "A plain metal door faces you to the east, near the alley's end. It's firmly shut.\r\u001b[27d>"]
[2.504, "o", "e"]
[0.090, "o", "x"]
[0.091, "o", "a"]
[0.090, "o", "m"]
[0.091, "o", "i"]
[0.090, "o", "n"]
[0.091, "o", "e"]
[0.090, "o", " "]
[0.091, "o", "d"]
[0.091, "o", "o"]
[0.090, "o", "o"]
[0.091, "o", "r"]
[0.090, "o", "\r\u001b[2d"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[2M\u001b[26dIt's a naked sheet of metal, a foot taller than you, as wide as your outstretched arms. No handle,\r\u001b[27d"]
[0.000, "o", "no keyhole, no label, no sign. No obvious way to open it at all, unless the black plate embedded\r\u001b[28d"]
[0.000, "o", "beside it will serve.\r\u001b[30d>"]
[2.413, "o", "e"]
[0.091, "o", "x"]
[0.090, "o", "a"]
[0.091, "o", "m"]
